{%- case gem_handle -%}

  {%- when 'navratana' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--navratana">
    <h2>What Belongs in Navratna</h2>
    <p>The Nine Gems of Navratna</p>
    <ul>
      <p>☉ Ruby — Vitality & Purpose</p>
      <p>☽ Pearl — Emotional Balance</p>
      <p>♂ Red Coral — Courage & Action</p>
      <p>☿ Emerald — Clarity & Communication</p>
      <p>♃ Yellow Sapphire — Wisdom & Growth</p>
      <p>♀ White Sapphire / Diamond — Harmony & Refinement</p>
      <p>♄ Blue Sapphire — Discipline & Stability</p>
      <p>☊ Hessonite — Discernment & Protection</p>
      <p>☋ Cat's Eye — Focus & Precision</p>
    </ul>
    <p>Each gemstone contributes its own presence.</p>
    <p>Together, they form one of the oldest and most recognised gemstone combinations in Vedic tradition.</p>
  </div>

  {%- when 'upratnas' -%}
  <div class="gem-tab gem-tab--upratnas">
    <h3>What Belongs in Upratnas</h3>
    <p>[Placeholder] Upratnas are the sanctioned substitutes for the nine primary Navratna gems. This collection includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>[Placeholder] Garnet — substitute for Ruby</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] Moonstone — substitute for Pearl</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] Red Jasper / Carnelian — substitute for Red Coral</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] Green Onyx / Peridot — substitute for Emerald</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] Citrine / Topaz — substitute for Yellow Sapphire</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] White Topaz / Opal — substitute for Diamond</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] Iolite / Amethyst — substitute for Blue Sapphire</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] Turquoise — substitute for Hessonite</li>
      <li>[Placeholder] Tiger's Eye — substitute for Cat's Eye</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {%- else -%}
  <div class="gem-tab">
    <p>[Placeholder] Content coming soon.</p>
  </div>

{%- endcase -%}
